  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Dancin' in the Street** (1 review): A slower tempo was used effectively, with John's vocal-melody inspired solo standing out [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **News Report**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-06-15** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 196 min; rated 1.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Files are encoded as AIF, which are larger than Wavs and harder to convert [4]\n- **deadco2024-06-15.McCormick**: source not stated; 15 songs; 201 min [2]. Said about its sound: The backup recording from the Zoom Q2n on a five-foot stand is transparent and clear [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Doug Haxall handled security and VIPs, while new friends Drew and Matteus shared the experience [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-06-15**: taped by Sir Chu Sonoran Dawg; transferred by Sir Chu Sonoran Dawg; source: AUF > Zoom iq7 > iPhone 14 [1]. Also: The recording lineage indicates the uploader converted original Wavs to AIF format [4]\n- **deadco2024-06-15.McCormick**: taped by Luke McCormick; transferred by Luke McCormick; source: Zoom Q2n on 5ft stand in taper section, Sec 103 [2]. Also: Primary Tascam DR40x rig distorted on bass hits, so backup Zoom Q2n was used [2]",
